# Active pre-push gate (BM-1): run the full /ship verification before any push,
# so the gate is enforced by structure, not memory -- on the free GitHub plan
# the CI workflows are dormant (ADR-007), making this the real gate. It mirrors
# CI exactly (typecheck -> lint -> tests -> build -> gitleaks -> npm audit).
#
# Emergency bypass: `git push --no-verify` (use sparingly; CI will still gate
# once active at /handoff).
# Run from a linked worktree, git exports GIT_DIR (an absolute
# .git/worktrees/<name> path) into this hook, and the harness tests that build
# throw-away repos then operate on THIS repository (they committed, branched and
# rewrote the shared config). Unset the plumbing variables so every child
# discovers its repository from its own cwd.
unset GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_PREFIX
npm run ship

# Receipt gate — review-before-push (ADR-064 / docs/blueprints/sdlc-chain.md, AC-1.1/1.2/1.6): require a
# content-bound `Reviewed: <scope> <tree-sha>` trailer for pushes that touch auth files,
# prisma/schema.prisma, app/api/** or lib/**. Runs AFTER `npm run ship` so a red build still
# fails first. Governance gate -- it fails OPEN on its own error (ADR-047) and only ever
# hard-rejects on an actually-missing or stale receipt. Deliberate skip: a
# `Gate-Skip: review-gate <reason>` trailer (recorded, loud, and permanent in git history).
# Per-link backout: delete this one line to disable this link; nothing else depends on it.
# ENABLED 2026-08-22, after six adversarial breadth passes (6 -> 5 -> 4 -> 3 -> 1 -> 1
# findings, all 20 in the gate code; the skills, evals, descriptions, router and docs drew
# zero across all six). Forks inherit main, so this is on by default for every fork, like
# the security floor. To turn this link off, comment this one line out -- nothing else
# depends on it, and the qa-gate link keeps working.
node .claude/hooks/review-gate.mjs
